 equipment assigned to area safe, orderly and in sanitary condition; reports needed repairs; maintain weight equipment to assure efficient operation. Organize and clean equipment and conduct preventative maintenance. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Good customer relation and service skills. Ability to work in a team and as an individual in a self-paced, task-oriented environment. Ability to follow instructions and enforce facility and University policies and rules. Dependable and responsible. Ability to be organized and cleanly. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current full-time student at the University of the Incarnate Word. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Working knowledge of fitness facilities, equipment, and tools. One or more years of work experience in the fitness and wellness industry. One or more years of work in customer service industry. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Current CPR and First Aid Certification. Work Hours Varies, flexible schedule. Physical Demands This position requires manual labor with the ability to lift 50 pounds. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1623PO Number of Vacancies 8 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness Salary $12 per hour Open Date 07/06/2026 Close Date 05/31/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pool position with hires expected throughout the academic year and as early as July 2026. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic 