    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30708": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | The Logos Student Newspaper Multimedia Journalist Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW The Logos Student Newspaper Multimedia Journalist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title The Logos Student Newspaper Multimedia Journalist Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Logos Student Newspaper Multimedia Journalist ( MMJ ) helps the editor and assistant editor, in producing The Logos, the student-run digital newspaper. The Logos Student Newspaper Multimedia Journalist reports to the Faculty Advisor for The Logos. This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment. Essential Functions Identify newsworthy events and story ideas. Gather information through research, observation, and interviews. Write news stories, features, and articles for various formats. Edit and proofread content for grammar, accuracy, and style. Conduct interviews, research, and write news stories, features, and other content for different platforms. Produce, edit, and manage audio, video, and photographic content. Assist in production of the newspaper. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Multimedia journalist should have good grammar skills, know Associated Press style, and have good photography skills. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Be a full-time UIW student during the 2026-27 academic year Have a minimum GPA of 2.5, with a 3.0 in the major discipline Be at least a sophomore (exceptions may be granted at the discretion of the Board) Required Work Experience No required work experience necessary Preferred Qualifications Preference given to students with previous high school or college journalistic experience (newspaper, yearbook, magazine, anthology, broadcasting class, website, etc.) Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Work Hours Up to twenty hours per week based on student availability. Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 25 pounds. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1552PO Number of Vacancies 3 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Faculty Advisor for the Logos Salary $12/hr Open Date 06/01/2026 Close Date 03/31/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Writing Sample Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate 