    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31628": {
      "title": "Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability-Student Assistant",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Ettling Center for Civic Leadership &amp; Sustainability-Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability-Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability-Student Assistant Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Student Assistant for the Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability provides clerical & programmatic support, including but not limited to: assisting office staff with mass marketing/publications/mail-outs, data entry, filing, customer service, social media & program support. The Student Assistant reports to the Director for the Ettling Center. This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program. Essential Functions Answer multi-phone line. Actively participate in daily operations (including programs and services) of the Center to ensure all assigned, operational, and support tasks are completed on a daily basis. Assist and support professional and part-time professional staff with the successful development, preparation, implementation, assessment, and completion of programs, services, and activities supported by the Center. Support the daily office needs of the Center by making copies, taking messages, collating, assisting with mailouts, development of flyers and other marketing materials, delivery and collection of mail. Engage in communication and customer service dialogue with administrators, faculty, staff, students, and community. Assist with the daily operations of the Cardinals’ Cupboard Food Pantry supported by the Ettling Center. Serve as a guide to the campus and local community members who may need assistance and/or escort to any UIW office on main campus. Communicate the mission, vision, and goals of the Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability programs to students, parents, staff, faculty, and global community partners; Participate in projects sponsored and hosted by the Ettling Center. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Ability to be organized and finish projects in a timely fashion. Communicate progress of tasks to peers and office supervisors. Ability to be responsible and reliable in maintaining a consistent work schedule. Exceptional customer service skills. Ability to learn specific and different policy and procedures associated with all aspects of the Ettling Center. Knowledgeable in Microsoft Word, PowerPoint, Excel, and Canva. Organization skills to keep proper records to include tracking of any visitors to the Center. Ability to maintain confidentiality and privacy of student/academic information and community members. Must be responsible and reliable in maintaining a consistent work schedule. Required Education Current UIW student. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Bilingual in English and Spanish. Prior experience in working with a non-profit or community based organization will be an asset . Customer service experience in a high volume setting. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None specified. Work Hours Monday through Fridays 8a-5p. Some early mornings, evening, and weekend opportunities may be available for specific projects during the year. Physical Demands Ability to lift and move 30 lbs. Ability to remain sitting for approximately 30 minutes at a time to complete daily tasks. Ability to host an informational table for approximately 30 minutes without interruption. May be required to support clean up of center-sponsored programs and activities which may be indoors and outdoors and may include wearing closed shoes, gloves, & protective eye-wear. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1672PO Number of Vacancies 8 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/24/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Director, Ettling Center for Civic Leadership & Sustainability Salary $11.00/hr Open Date 08/12/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
