    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31495": {
      "title": "New Student Programs Student Assistant",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | New Student Programs Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW New Student Programs Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title New Student Programs Student Assistant Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The New Student Programs Office Assistant provides customer service to students, faculty, and staff. The Office Assistant for New Student Programs works in conjunction with New Student Program peer mentors to better serve students and other members of the UIW community. The New Student Programs Office Assistant will report to the Director of New Student Programs. Essential Functions Assists in planning and coordinating of purposeful programs and activities for new students. Supports the New Student Programs team to build community in The Landing. Enhances the student experience by assisting in providing student resources for student success. Assists the Graduate Assistant and Director in compiling content for flyers and social media. Collaborates on and designs content for the notification boards located in The Landing. Coordinates and manages departmental resources. Maintains inventory of student snacks and other items provided in The Landing. The Office Assistant is responsible for the general cleanliness, organization, and appearance of The Landing and NSP storage spaces. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Ability to finish projects and/or communicate progress to peers and leadership in a timely manner. Excellent customer service skills. Ability to learn specific and different policy and procedures associated with the Office of New Student Programs. Intermediate knowledge in Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Canva. Intermediate level data entry skills to maintain records, including tracking visitors to the Landing and at NSP events. Ability to work and communicate effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Completed 1+ years at UIW as a student. Required Work Experience Experience is not required, training is available. Preferred Qualifications Customer service experience in a high-volume setting. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Monday – Friday 8:30 a.m. – 5 p.m.; 8-10 hours per week. Some early mornings, evenings and weekends required for specific meetings or events during the year. Physical Demands Ability to lift 30 lbs. Able to stand, bend, and reach to perform various tasks as needed. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1637PO Number of Vacancies 2 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Director of New Student Programs Salary Open Date 07/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required D