    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31630": {
      "title": "Student Employee Front Desk Assistant",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Employee Front Desk Assistant Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Employee Front Desk Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Employee Front Desk Assistant Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary Student Employee Front Desk Assistant will work to support the front desk staff at the Rosenberg School of Optometry. This position will report to the Assistant Clinic Support Manager. Position will located at: Datapoint Location, 9725 Datapoint Drive Bowden Location, 2547 E. Commerce Street Essential Functions Answering phones, Checking voicemail. Making patient appointments. Assisting with the patient check in process. Patient appointment confirmation calls. Printing medical records from previous EMR . Scanning them into current EMR . Other duties as assigned Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Ability to self-start daily tasks Ability to multi-tasking Flexibility Verbal and written communication Customer Service Organization Attention to Detail Scheduling, Word Processing Professionalism Quality Focus Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW student. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Previous work experience in a medical office is preferred. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Yearly HIPAA training. This training will be provided by employer and must be completed successfully with in 14 business days of employment. Work Hours 10-20 hrs. per week. Datapoint Location, 9725 Datapoint Drive: Monday- Friday hours are available. Bowden Location, 2547 E. Commerce Street: Monday-Saturday hours are available. Saturdays are required. Physical Demands Typical for office work. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1674PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/24/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Clinic Support Manager Salary $11.00 Open Date 08/14/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
