    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31199": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Graduate Assistant - Sports Medicine Administrative Assistant Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Graduate Assistant - Sports Medicine Administrative Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant - Sports Medicine Administrative Assistant Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary Graduate Assistant for the Sports Medicine Department (Athletic Training), performs duties that include: managing the EMR system; managing athletic training rooms, and performing other duties as assigned. The Graduate Assistant Sports Medicine Department (Athletic Training) reports directly to the Associate Director of Athletics-Sports Medicine. Essential Functions Manage, organize, and maintain assigned athletic training rooms, equipment, supplies and inventory. Maintain computerized injury, treatment, incident, insurance, and medication forms and/or databases. Communicate with department heads. Manage check-in and check-out processes for all physician visits on campus and sports medicine physicals. Facilitate Physicians clinic by providing physicians with equipment or supplies needed to conduct their assessment or visit. Scan documentation into sports medicine shared drive and within EMR patient profiles. Maintain documentation compliance within EMR system. Management of a paper documentation. Ensure each athletic training room is well-stocked with appropriate inventory for daily-use and has maintained sanitary standards of cleanliness each week. Assistance in other duties as it pertains to the daily operations of athletic training facilities; daily cleaning, practice/game set-up and break down assistance. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Excellent customer service. Exceptional organization and detailed-orientated skills. Maintain professionalism at all times. Proficiency in Microsoft Office. Outstanding communication skills, written and verbal with the ability to communicate well with professional staff and peers. Ability to multi-task and be both, team player and self starter. Ability to use basic office equipment. Ability to communicate both verbally and orally. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Bachelor’s Degree in Rehab Science or related field or Graduate student enrolled in Masters Science of Athletic Training program at UIW . Required Work Experience Clinical hours in sports medicine or related field. Preferred Qualifications None. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Must have a valid driver license, driving record that is insurable by UIW insurance carrier, and be at least 21 years of age, as required to drive for UIW . Work Hours Monday – Friday with extended hours as needed to meet departmental goals. Physical Demands May require lifting of heavy objects items (supplies, inventory items, etc.) Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1607PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Senior Associate Athletic Director/Student Well Being Salary $2,100 + Tuition Waiver Open Date 06/17/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a UIW Graduate student? Yes No Applied - Awaiting Acceptance * What is the major of your Graduate Degree? (Open Ended Question) * How many clinical hours do you have in sports medicine or a related field? (Open Ended Question) 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
