    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31027": {
      "title": "Athletics Facilities  and Operations Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Athletics Facilities  and Operations Graduate Assistant Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Athletics Facilities  and Operations Graduate Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Athletics Facilities  and Operations Graduate Assistant Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The University of the Incarnate Word is seeking qualified applicants for the position of Athletics Facilities and Operations Graduate Assistant. The Facilities and Operations Graduate Assistant is responsible for assisting with the day-to-day facilities and operations of the Athletic Department. The position will report to the Assistant Athletic Director for Administration. This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students. Essential Functions Assist with the facility scheduling of varsity practices, games, and third party rentals. Assist with the scheduling and coordinating of visiting team practices and facility needs for selected sports. Assist with summer camps, including registration, financial reports, deposits, and assisting with walk-up registrations. Assist with the review and reconciliation of all third party facility rental agreements and payments. Assist with coordinating repairs and maintenance of all facilities equipment. Assist with summer camps, including registration, financial reports, deposits, and assisting with walk-up registrations. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Strong writing and communication skills. Self-starter and ability to work without supervision. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Able to work nights and weekends. Demonstrable teamwork and team-building skills. Demonstrable priority and setting and organizational skills. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW graduate student. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Experience with athletic game operations. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Must have a valid Texas driver’s license and be insurable with UIW’s insurance carrier. Work Hours Monday – Friday up to 25 hours per week. Some weekends and holidays. Physical Demands Ability to lift equipment, tools, and/or materials weighing up to 25 pounds waist high. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1586PO Number of Vacancies 3 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/15/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Athletic Director for Administration Salary $2,100 + Tuition Waiver Open Date 05/13/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Student Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a UIW Graduate student? Yes No Applied - Awaiting Acceptance 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
