      "title": "Communication Arts Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Communication Arts Graduate Assistant Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Communication Arts Graduate Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Communication Arts Graduate Assistant Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Communications Arts Graduate Assistant is responsible for assisting in Department of Communication Arts media production, special projects, and more. The Graduate Assistant reports to the Communication Arts Department Chair. Essential Functions Assist the Communication Arts Department Chair & supervising faculty with special projects, including data collection. Assist with content development and production of SMD social media. Adhere to all UIW branding standards, style guides and web standards. Understand and represent the mission and vision of Communication Arts, School of Media and Design, and the University of the Incarnate Word. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Ability to operate in desktop publishing, Adobe Photoshop, etc. Ability to operate in video editing, Adobe Premiere. Ability to email marketing, photography, and social media development. Excellent oral and written communication and interpersonal skills. Excellent ability to interact with a variety of stakeholders such as faculty, alumni, and students. Proficiency in Microsoft Office products. Proficiency in Adobe Suite (InDesign, AfterEffects, Photoshop, Premiere, etc.). Excellent organizational and time-management skills. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW Communication Arts Graduate Student. Required Work Experience Experience with Adobe Photoshop, Adobe Premiere, and social media development. Preferred Qualifications Experience in media production and marketing. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Monday through Friday 8am- 5pm. Physical Demands Ability to lift equipment, tools, and/or materials weighing up to 25 lbs. waist-high. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1668PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/24/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Communication Arts Department Chair (Darlene Carbajal) Salary Tuition Credit Open Date 08/10/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW Communication Arts graduate student in good academic standing? Yes No * Please describe your experience with Adobe Photoshop, Adobe Premiere and social media development. (Open Ended Question) 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 7