    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31374": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Red the Cardinal - UIW Mascot Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Red the Cardinal - UIW Mascot Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Red the Cardinal - UIW Mascot Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary As Red the Cardinal, the official mascot of the University of the Incarnate Word, you will serve as an enthusiastic and engaging ambassador for the university. This role requires a positive, energetic, and professional demeanor while representing UIW at a variety of campus and community events. Responsibilities include wearing the mascot costume and interacting with diverse audiences to promote school spirit, foster community engagement, and enhance the university’s public image. Red the Cardinal reports to the Advertising, Branding and Licensing Mangager. Essential Functions Duties may include: Distributing promotional materials. Serving as a sign holder. Performing in front of crowds through dancing and interactive appearances, participating in games and activities. Attending charitable and community functions. Supporting university branding, marketing, and outreach initiatives. Additional event-related duties may be assigned as needed to support UIW programs and special events. Our Ideal Mascot Performer is: Professional Punctual Team oriented Energetic/Enthusiastic Approachable Committed Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities The student chosen to play Red the Cardinal will be responsible for, but not limited to, attending sporting events in costume to entertain fans of all ages, be an uplifting off-field presence to the athletes and staff during competitions, and serve as a spirited public representative for the University. The mascot may plan, develop, and implement dance routines, skits, and other activities in collaboration with the Office of Communications and Brand Marketing. An individual functioning as the mascot should have the ability to bring the character to life in order to energize the spectators. This includes: Being responsible and accountable to appearance schedules- arriving on time and remaining for the duration of a shift; Exhibiting strong non-verbal communication skills; Demonstrating an outgoing performance personality with an ability to interact with spectators; Fostering a fun and energetic atmosphere with spectator and at events; Possessing a creative and humorous personality while maintaining a professional demeanor; Providing high quality customer service; Maintaining independent and self-motivated style, while remaining flexible and adaptable; Caring for the mascot costume and props when possessing it; Being athletically and physically fit to wear costume and perform for duration of events; Must be able to comfortably and safely fit in the mascot costume; Willing to work extended and/or irregular hours including nights and weekends, both indoors and outdoors. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Must maintain an equal commitment to both academic responsibilities and responsibilities as the Red the Cardinal – UIW mascot. Required Education Must be an enrolled UIW student Be enrolled in no less than 12 credit hours per semester (full-time) Maintain a minimum 2.5 GPA Required Work Experience Previous experience in spirit, dance, cheer or having served as a school mascot, a plus. Preferred Qualifications Candidates should plan to participate in a tryout (details included with acceptance of application) Applicants should demonstrate awareness and sensitivity that embraces and supports working within a diverse, multicultural community. The candidate must show the ability to work with the Office of Communications and Brand Marketing as well as the UIW Department of Athletics. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Part-time and event based. Willing to work with mascot staff availability/schedules. Hours will vary, including working at after hours events, sporting events and other activities. Must be available for at least 2 UIW home football games. Physical Demands Must be in good physical shape, able to fit the Red the Mascot costume (height between 5’7”-6’2”) Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1634PO Number of Vacancies 2 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/01/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Advertising, Branding and Licensing Mangager Salary $14.50/hr Open Date 07/08/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Do you have a CUMULATIVE GPA of 2.5 or higher? Yes No * Please describe your previous experience in a dance, spirit, cheer group, or as a school mascot. (Open Ended Question) 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
