    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31673": {
      "title": "Student Assistant for Testing Services",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Assistant for Testing Services Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Assistant for Testing Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Assistant for Testing Services Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Staff Assistant provides support to the Coordinator of Testing in the daily operations of the Testing Center. Serves as the first line of contact with students and faculty. Administers faculty make-up examinations, national computer based exams such as CLEP , THEA and HESI -A2. Assists Coordinator and Specialist during testing and supervises the day’s exams as required. Assists Coordinator in creating reports. Serves as an information source to students and faculty about the services offered at University Testing Services. Essential Functions Interaction with students, faculty, and administrators in a professional manner. Assist with reception duties as necessary. Facilitate administration of faculty make-up exams. Set up CLEP server and work stations as needed. Proctor computer-based exams. Enter data into testing spreadsheets, as requested by Coordinator. Assist with the creation of monthly reports. Ensure security of make-up exams by following established procedures. Maintain confidentiality of student testing records. Comply with University Testing Services policies and procedures. Perform other duties as required. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Proficiency in standard computer skills (esp. Microsoft 365, and internet browser). Extreme attention to detail. Understands the importance of confidentiality regarding student records. Familiarity with the university’s student support services and departments. Required Education Current UIW graduate or undergraduate student. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications None. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Ability to work at least 12 hours per week. Flexibility to work during Testing Center hours of operation: Monday to Friday, 8am-5pm. Physical Demands Typical for job position. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1527PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 03/02/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) 05/29/2026 Reports to Testing Coordinator Salary 11 p/h Open Date 01/26/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security 