    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31521": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Academic Peer Tutors for Rosenberg School of Optometry Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Academic Peer Tutors for Rosenberg School of Optometry Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Academic Peer Tutors for Rosenberg School of Optometry Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary Academic Peer Tutors for Rosenberg School of Optometry assist students in the Rosenberg School of Optometry with selected coursework during the 2026-2027 year. Tutoring is either done individually, in small groups or in a class-wide review session format depending on need. Tutors are being sought specifically for Clinical Optometry I, Optics, Anatomy, Neuroanatomy, Organ Pathology, and Ocular Anatomy and Physiology I. Academic Peer Tutors report to the Director, Academic Success. This is a student position open to current Rosenberg School of Optometry students who have completed the course(s) they wish to tutor with a grade of B or higher. Essential Functions Provide support and tutoring knowledge in a small or large group or individual setting; Share knowledge of course materials in selected coursework; Develop a strong working relationship with assigned students; Consult with faculty about topics students most need assistance with Keep accurate records of hours worked Perform other duties as assigned Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Comfort with knowledge in the course material in courses that you choose to tutor; Ability to work patiently with others and explain sometimes complex concepts; Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures; Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA Required Education Current Rosenberg School of Optometry student who has completed the course(s) they wish to tutor with a grade of B- or higher; Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Comfort working with students individually or in small groups (5-10 students) or large groups (10 or more students). Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Arranged between students for individual and small group sessions. Large group sessions are generally held early afternoons on weekends or weekday evenings. Physical Demands Typical for this position. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1654PO Number of Vacancies 15 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 09/14/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Director, Academic Success Salary Begins at $11 and hour but depends on work experience with UIW and UIWRSO Open Date 07/28/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current optometry student at the Rosenberg School of Optometry? Yes, I am a First-Year Student Yes, I am a Second-Year Student Yes, I am a Third-Year Student Yes, I am a Fourth-Year Student No, I am not a UIW Student at RSO 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
