      "title": "Fashion Management - Student Assistant - 2026/2027",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Fashion Management - Student Assistant - 2026/2027 Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Fashion Management - Student Assistant - 2026/2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Fashion Management - Student Assistant - 2026/2027 Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Student Assistant for Fashion Management primarily works as a teaching assistant in Fashion Studio classes and assists faculty and staff with day-to-day tasks as needed by the department. The Student Assistant reports to the Fashion Management Faculty. Essential Functions Assists faculty in Fashion Design Studio classes. Typing. Filing. Answering phones. Assists faculty, staff, and student. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Working knowledge of Word, Excel, Powerpoint, Photoshop, and Illustrator. Excellent interpersonal skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and reliability. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW fashion student. Eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study program Successfully completed the following course: FMGT 1310. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Previous office experience. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours M-F, between 8:00 am and 5:00 pm Physical Demands Ability to lift 10lbs or more Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1604PO Number of Vacancies 5 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/10/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Faculty Salary $11.00/hr Open Date 06/22/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know * Are you a current UIW student in the Fashion Management program and successfully completed the course FMGT 1310: Apparel Construction? Yes No 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
