    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31334": {
      "title": "eSports Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student)",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | eSports Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW eSports Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title eSports Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The eSports Coach (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for coaching the eSports team during the Fall and Spring semesters. eSports offers competitions at the Club Sport level in the following games: Smash Bros, Overwatch, League of Legends, Rocket League, Counter Strike: Global Offensive, Tom Clancy’s Rainbow Six Siege, Dragon Ball FighterZ, Street Fighter V and others. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness in the Club Sports Program. This is a student position open to current UIW graduate students. Essential Functions Essential functions include: Attend all meetings; Direct practices; Assist in the running of UIW eSports discord server Train athletes on strategies and techniques; Motivate student-athletes; Supervise travel, competitions and meets; Responsible for keeping balanced budgets; Ensure student-athletes are maintaining GPA ; Assist with running and leading funding raising events; Create new relationships with sponsors as well as attend community service events; Work with Club Sports supervisor to better the program by, but not limited to, assisting with marketing/ recruiting for the team; Annual review following each season worked; Perform other duties as assigned Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Strong communication and interpersonal skills; Knowledge of multiple eSports games Ability to plan efficient practices involving individual instruction and team development; Commitment to student-athlete welfare and academic success; Commitment to University rules; Ability to assess team needs and develop goal-oriented action plans; Excellent organizational and time-management skills; Excellent marketing skills; Ability to meet during work hours with athletes, trainer, and supervisors during the academic year; Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures; Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA Required Education Current UIW graduate student Required Work Experience At least one (1) year coaching experience or participation in a college eSports program Successful competition and/or coaching in several different eSport games Preferred Qualifications None. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations CPR and First Aid Certification (if expired, must be completed within 3 months of employment) Work Hours 20 hours per week required; Practices and games/tournaments are on nights and weekends Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 25 pounds. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1620PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness Salary Open Date 07/06/2026 Close Date 05/31/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Multi Media Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you a UIW Graduate student? Yes No Applied - Awaiting Acceptance Are you currently CPR and First Aid certified? Yes No No, but I will complete within the timeframe stipulated in the job posting as required. Are you able to work evenings and/or weekends? Yes No Have you ever managed a budget? Give details. (Open Ended Question) Describe your knowledge, skills, and experience related to the essential duties and responsibilities of the position. (Open Ended Question) Describe what makes you qualified for this position. (Open Ended Question) 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
