      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Strength and Conditioning Coach (Graduate Assistant) Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Strength and Conditioning Coach (Graduate Assistant) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Strength and Conditioning Coach (Graduate Assistant) Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Strength and Conditioning Coach (Graduate Assistant) will assist the with strength and conditioning for all UIW athletes. The Strength and Conditioning Coach (Graduate Assistant) reports to the Head Strength and Conditioning Coach. Essential Functions Responsible for all scheduling, training, testing, organization and administration of teams as assigned by the Head Strength & Conditioning Coach, this may include educating student-athletes in areas of nutrition and banned substances. Assist directly with the football program as needed. Responsible for maintenance of weight room, suplement areas and all equipment. Work effectively with all Sports Medicine, Sport coaches, Administration and University staff. Perform any other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Sincere desire and passion to assist student-athletes in reaching their athletic performance and personal goals. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Demonstrate a willingness to enforce weight room, UIW athletic department rules/ policies, and NCAA rules at all times. Demonstrated proficiency in teaching the Olympic Lifts and their variations. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education UIW graduate student, or accepted to UIW graduate program. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications One (1) year working in a collegiate strength & conditioning program. Prior experience as a collegiate student-athlete. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Documented progress toward any or all of the following certifications: S.C.C.C, USAW , C.S.C.S Work Hours 25 hours per week, varied hours. Some night & weekend hours will be required at select points of the calendar year. Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 45 lbs. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1554PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 06/01/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Head Strength and Conditioning Coach Salary $2,100 Stipend + Tuition Waiver Open Date 04/16/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a UIW Graduate student? Yes No Applied - Awaiting Acceptance 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University o