    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31487": {
      "title": "Student Assistant for Admissions Office",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Assistant for Admissions Office Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Assistant for Admissions Office Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Assistant for Admissions Office Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Student Assistant for the Admissions Office assists with all tasks, processes and events of the Office of Admissions. The Student Assistant provides excellent customer service to prospective students, their families, and the community as a whole. The Student Assistant reports to the Assistant Director of Campus Events. This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment. Essential Functions Works in a fast paced, high profile environment. Manages front desk, lobby/presentation room and UIW Welcome Center duties. Provides excellent customer service to prospective students, their families, and other guests. Provides campus tours for 1 to 25 guests. Answers multi-line phone system; transfers calls to appropriate department or personnel for assistance. Provides general University/Admissions information. Assists with scheduling daily tours and counselor appointments. Assists with errands across campus daily. Assists with mail pick up and delivery between Admissions office, UIW post office, and other campus offices. Assists with packaging and labeling of recruitment materials, student packets, counselor materials, and other mail-outs. Assists with preparation for various admissions events. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Excellent interpersonal skills. Self-motivated with proper behavioral etiquette. Proficient in Microsoft Office 365 and OneDrive. Basic computer and office equipment skills. Ability to work well with others. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Strong verbal communication skills. Able to interact with staff in various positions (i.e., Directors, Vice Presidents, faculty, etc.). Ability to follow instructions and take direction. Ability to adhere to office dress code/uniform expectations. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW student. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Bilingual (Spanish) preferred. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Flexible shifts between the hours of 8am-5pm. Must be able to work flexible schedules during evenings and weekends when needed. Must be able to work Spring Break, some student holidays and Summer Sessions. Physical Demands Ability to regularly lift, push, and pull up to 20 lbs of recruiting materials. Ability to move about and actively engage with others during event preparation, execution of event, and post event activities. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1650PO Number of Vacancies 7 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/03/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Director of Campus Events Salary $11.00/hr Open Date 07/14/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
