    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31777": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Music Minister Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Music Minister Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Music Minister Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Student Music Minister is part of a team that serves at the 11 AM Mass as a member of and musical leader for the Laudate Choir. As a leadership team member of the Music Ministry, the Music Minister also serves at major university liturgies and prayer events sponsored by University Mission and Ministry. Essential Functions Ministerial presence and service at the 11 AM Sunday Mass. Serves at major university liturgies and prayer events sponsored by UMM . Fosters a sense of community, service and ministerial investment within the members of the Laudate Choir, and Music Ministry as a whole. Supports the spiritual growth of the Music Ministry and Campus Ministry through the participation in, and planning of, retreats. Assists the DMM and Liturgy & Music Assistant in establishing a communal repertoire of sung prayer for the university community. Assists the DMM and Liturgy & Music Assistant in administrative duties such as, but not limited to: communication within the choir, weekly rehearsal plan, copyright filing, maintaining music, assisting with area fellowship gatherings. Practices their craft regularly to ensure preparation for rehearsals and liturgical prayer. Attends Music Ministry and Divisional Formation Sessions. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Ability to proficiently read music: identify rhythms and pitches, including matching pitch. Applied skills in voice, guitar, piano, or another instrument. Basic computer skills in Microsoft Office. Openness and self-motivation to seek out opportunities that will supplement and broaden the minister’s entry level experience/knowledge of music/liturgical ministry. Required Education Current UIW student. Required Work Experience Previous experience singing or playing in a music ministry, choral ensemble, or instrumental ensemble such as a band or choir (e.g. parish choir, UIW Cardinal Chorale/Singers, UIW Laudate Choir). Preferred Qualifications n/a. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations n/a. Work Hours Sunday – Thursday; 10 hours a week. Physical Demands Must be able to lift and/or move at least 15 lbs (i.e., equipment and materials related to the position or within the office). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1639PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 09/14/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Director of Music Ministries and Liturgy Salary Open Date 09/04/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Supplemental Questions Required fields are