computer experience, including but not limited to Microsoft Outlook, Word, Excel and PowerPoint. Ability to effectively maintain confidentiality. Ability to effectively communicate. Ability to complete tasks with limited supervision. Strong attention to detail. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW student approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study program. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Experience with creating digital media content (Photoshop, Canva, etc.) Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours This position is approximately 10 hours per week. The schedule assigned will be during Monday through Friday, 8am to 5pm, with flexibility based on events, trainings, outreach, etc. Schedule will be flexible based on availability and school schedules. Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 25lbs of office/event materials. Ability to reach overhead, bend, squat to retrieve office/events materials. Ability to push/pull event carts holding up to 50 lbs. Ability to actively engage in events for extended periods of time. Ability to regularly move about campus to attend meetings, events, and presentations. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1642PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/01/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Director of Title IX Salary $11.00/hr Open Date 07/09/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy