    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31634": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Shipping/Receiving Warehouse Clerk Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Shipping/Receiving Warehouse Clerk Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. N/A. Position Details Position Information Position Title Shipping/Receiving Warehouse Clerk UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Shipping and Receiving Warehouse Clerk will be responsible for incoming and outgoing shipments, verifying and maintaining records, preparing items for shipment and coordinating transportation arrangements. The Shipping and Receiving Warehouse Clerk reports to the Fixed Asset Specialist. Benefits UIW has been identified year after year as one of the nation’s Great Colleges to Work For based on employee feedback. UIW offers an outstanding benefits package for full-time employees that includes medical, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts, numerous paid holidays, vacation and sick leave. Tuition benefits include UIW tuition waivers, tuition exchange programs and Brainpower Connection discounts for employees and dependents. Retirement benefits include 403b retirement plans with a 7% employer match, plus a retirement health solution. We also offer employer-paid Life/AD&D, long-term disability, pet insurance, an Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ), wellness programs, employee discount program, Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligibility and more! Please refer to the Human Resources webpage for additional details on our benefits and eligibility. Job Duties Job Duty Name Receiving Packages/Freight Items Description of Job Duties Receive incoming shipments, verify contents against purchase orders or invoices. Inspect received goods for damages or discrepancies. Utilize SC Logic package tracking and inventory system to distribute and track assets. Work closely with carriers and suppliers on a daily basis, including but not limited to Fed Ex, UPS , DHL , Amazon, etc. Perform other duties as assigned. Job Duty Name Shipping Description of Job Duties Prepare outgoing shipments by assembling items, verifying quantities and packing securely for transportation. Generate shipping labels and ensure correct shipping documentation is included. Coordinate with internal departments and carriers to schedule pickups and deliveries. Provide shipment status updates and tracking information as needed. Job Duty Name Inventory Management Description of Job Duties Maintain accurate records of inventory levels and locations. Conduct regular inventory counts and reconciling discrepancies. Assist in the annual audit process of fixed asset tagging and required inventory items. Job Duty Name General Description of Job Duties Communicate effectively with vendors, carriers, and internal departments to resolve issues and ensure timely shipments. Adhere to safety protocols and guidelines in handling and storing materials. Ensure compliance with shipping and receiving regulations and procedures. Maintain a clean and organized work area. Maintain and update tracking system on all assets. Cross-train with colleagues to ensure best route process for daily campus runs. Deliver assets to departments via golf cart or UIW vehicle, as appropriate based on size of asset and the delivery location (including satellites). Inspect assigned vehicles daily for maintenance and safety concerns. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Ability to work efficiently and multitask. Strong attention to detail to ensure accuracy in recording and documenting shipments. Clear and effective communication with supplies, carriers and internal departments. Proficient in basic computer skills. Ability to effectively work individually and within a team environment. Ability to learn and safely use pallet jacks, and potentially a forklift. Good problem-solving abilities. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education High School diploma or GED equivalent. Required Work Experience At least three (3) months of experience in a warehouse or distribution environment or relevant area such as mail delivery, packaging, and inventory control. Office experience will be considered. Preferred Qualifications Forklift and pallet jack experience. Familiarity with inventory management software and shipping platforms (e.g., UPS , FedEx, Amazon, etc.) Knowledge of safety regulations and procedures in a warehouse environment. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Must have a valid driver license, driving record that is insurable by UIW insurance carrier, and be at least 21 years of age, as required to drive vehicles and golf carts for UIW . Work Hours Mon-Fri 8am to 5pm with occasional extended hours as needed to meet departmental goals. Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 45lbs packages. Ability to reach overhead, bend, and squat to process ingoing/ outgoing shipments. Ability to push/pull pallet jacks, carts, and wagon holding up to 100 lbs +. May involve exposure to varying temperatures and loud noises, typical of a warehouse environment. Ability to regularly move about warehouse space and campus locations throughout the shift to process and deliver packages on main campus, as well as satellite locations. Ability to safely maneuver vehicles and golf carts during standard shift. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number AS2301PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Full Time Job Category Staff  (non-exempt) Desired Start Date 09/16/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Director of Procurement and Other Support Services Salary $15.00 per hour Open Date 08/17/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant N/A. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Title IX This position is considered a “Responsible Employee” under Title IX federal regulations and “Mandatory Reporter” under Texas state law and the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. As a Mandatory Reporter, this position requires you as the employee to promptly report any incident that you witness or receive information about Title IX violations. These reporting responsibilities are set out in the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Letter of Recommendation 1 Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UIW Website HigherEdJobs.com Indeed LinkedIn WorkplaceDiversity.com HispanicDiversity.com BlackJobCenter.com WomensJobCenter.com VeteransConnect.com Personal Referral Employee Referral Other If you selected other, please tell us where? (Open Ended Question) * What is the highest level of education you have achieved? Less than High School Education or GED equivalent High School Education or GED equivalent HS/GED + Trade School Some College * Indicate your experience working in a warehouse or distribution environment or relevant area such as mail delivery, packaging, and inventory control. Note that office experience will be considered. Less than 3 months experience in a warehouse/distribution environment or relevant area 3-6 months experience in a warehouse/distribution environment or relevant area 7-11 months experience in a warehouse/distribution environment or relevant area 1 year of experience or more in a warehouse/distribution environment or relevant area At least 3 months of office experience * Describe your experience, if any, working with a forklift and/or pallet jack. (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently have a valid driver's license AND are you at least 21 years of age, as required to drive for UIW? No Yes, I have a valid driver license and I am at least 21 years old 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
