    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31498": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | New Student Programs Peer Mentor Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW New Student Programs Peer Mentor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title New Student Programs Peer Mentor Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The New Student Programs ( NSP ) Peer Mentor is an upper-level student (1+ years completed as a post-high school college student) who assists in mentoring first-year in college and transfer students to acclimate themselves to the university setting. The NSP Peer Mentor helps connect new students with university resources, initiates social and academic opportunities, and helps provide a holistic experience for first-year and transfer students. The New Student Programs ( NSP ) Peer Mentor reports to the Director of New Student Programs. Essential Functions Peer Mentorship : Provides mentorship to students in academic and college skill-building, navigating classes and accessing university resources. Meets with mentees to connect and guide them through their first year at UIW . Serves as a role model for first-year and transfer students by encouraging and modeling a successful balance of academic and college life, actively participating in classes and campus activities, maintaining a 3.0 Grade Point Average ( GPA ), and being an active member of the UIW community. Community Development: Maintains a strong presence in the NSP student lounge by maintaining office hours (10-12 hours per week), facilitating events, and being available during high-need periods such as class registration and finals. Takes the initiative to get to know visitors to the NSP lounge and events by engaging in conversation and encouraging participation in activities. Maintains a visible role on campus and is available and approachable to students. Assists in planning and coordinating purposeful NSP programs and activities for students. Other Duties: Attends and participates in peer mentor training and meetings organized by the Director of New Student Programs. Maintains frequent communication with other peer mentors, Director of New Student Programs ( NSP ), the NSP Graduate Assistant, and other office staff. Participates in Fall and Spring Commencement ceremonies. Assists the Director of New Student Programs with events related to the UIW Parent and Family Association. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Intermediate skills in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Intermediate skills in Canva and different social media platforms. Ability to learn and enact specific policies and procedures associated with the Office of New Student Programs. Ability to work in a team-driven environment. Intermediate data entry skills to maintain records, including tracking visitors to the NSP lounge and events. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current upper level student (1+ years completed as a post-high school college student). Minimum 3.0 GPA requirement. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Experience in high volume customer service environment. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Monday – Friday, between 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m., up to 15 hours a week. Evening and weekend hours may be scheduled due to NSP program and event commitments. Physical Demands Must be able to lift up to 20 lbs., stand, bend, and reach to perform various tasks as needed. Must be able to navigate campus. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1636PO Number of Vacancies 5 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Director of New Student Programs Salary Open Date 07/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31786": {
      "title": "President's Office Student Assistant",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | President&#39;s Office Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW President's Office Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title President's Office Student Assistant Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Student Assistant supports the Office of the President by performing general office tasks and hospitality for office guests. The Student Assistant reports to the Senior Advisor to the President for Communications and Operations. Essential Functions Assist with daily office tasks, including reception, hospitality and clerical support. Greet guests and represent the Office of the President in a professional and friendly manner. Maintain professional appearance File, copy, and scan documents as needed. Collect mail and deliveries and track correspondence. Maintain storage room, inventory and restock items as necessary. Run errands on the Broadway campus. Assist with special event and meeting preparation. Support vehicle maintenance management. Support parking reservations for guests. Ready and drive the golf cart in accordance with University and department guidelines. This may include opportunities to work on special projects remotely. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Represent the University of the Incarnate Word professionally and proudly in every interaction in the Office of the President. Communicate clearly, effectively and respectfully to staff and guests. Maintain discretion and confidentiality in all matters. Be punctual and manage time effectively. Experience with common computer applications, including Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), Cardinal Apps, and select web-based programs. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW student approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study program. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Previous work as a student worker, customer service representative or in a guest-facing role Bilingual (English/Spanish) or Spanish proficiency. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations A valid driver’s license, driving record that is insurable by UIW insurance carrier, as required to drive for UIW , this is needed to drive golf car around campus. Work Hours Availability during normal business hours, Monday – Friday, 8 am – 5 pm during the academic year. Depending on eligibility, may work up to but not exceed 20 hours per week. Work schedule to be determined, based on student schedule. Physical Demands Must be able to life 20 pounds Must be able to sit or stand for long periods of time. Must have the ability to work at a computer for an extended period of time. Must be able to regularly navigate campus to run errands. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1684PO Number of Vacancies 2 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Senior Advisor to the President for Communications and Operations. Salary $11.25/ hour Open Date 09/07/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, 