    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31329": {
      "title": "Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness (Student)",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness (Student) Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness (Student) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pool position with hires expected throughout the academic year and as early as July 2026. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness (Student) Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness is responsible for teaching classes for Sports and Wellness facilities, including water aerobics, group aerobics, group swim lessons, and individual swim lessons. The Student Instructor for Sports and Wellness reports to the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness. This is a student position open to current UIW students. Essential Functions Teach classes to students of all abilities and performing related administrative duties. Conduct classes for students, faculty, staff, community members, and Collegiate Club Sport Athletes. Complete daily walkthroughs of the facility. Informs administration of issues and is responsible for ensuring the aerobic equipment is functional and up to standards. Keep up with current trends and standards in their field of instruction. Understand and represent the mission and vision of UIW and UIWSports and Wellness. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Possess the skills and expertise necessary to instruct student, faculty, and staff in the skills of their specialty. Good customer relation, communication, and interpersonal skills. Effective instruction techniques and skills. Thorough knowledge of their field including, strategies, techniques, and progression. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW Student Required Work Experience Two (2) or more years’ experience teaching in their specialty/certification in an exercise environment Preferred Qualifications None. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Certification in instruction by a nationally recognized organization; CPR and First Aid Certification Work Hours Available weekends and evenings as duties required. Required to cover special events, holidays and school break schedules as required by the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness. Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 25 pounds. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1615PO Number of Vacancies 8 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Director of Sports and Wellnesstor Salary $20 per hour, limited hours Open Date 07/06/2026 Close Date 05/31/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant This is a pool position with hires expected throughout the academic year and as early as July 2026. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Letter of Recommendation 1 Student Class Schedule Evidence of Required Certification(s) Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Letter of Recommendation 2 Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you currently CPR and First Aid certified? Yes No No, but I will complete within the timeframe stipulated in the job posting as required. * Are you currently certified in aerobic instruction by a nationally certified organization? Yes No No, but will complete within 6 months of employment. * Describe your knowledge, skills, and experience related to the essential duties and responsibilities of the position. (Open Ended Question) * Please list the certifications you currently hold. (Open Ended Question) * Please list the type of classes you are interested in teaching. (Open Ended Question) 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
