    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31660": {
      "title": "Student Assistant for Athletic Training (Work-Study)",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Assistant for Athletic Training (Work-Study) Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Assistant for Athletic Training (Work-Study) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Assistant for Athletic Training (Work-Study) Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Student Assistant for Athletic Training will be responsible for the organization and management of athletic training services to various UIW student-athletes and teams under the supervision of the Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine. This position is funded by the Federal Work-Study program and is open to UIW students who are approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study Program. Essential Functions Assist the sports medicine staff as needed to aide in delivery of athletic training services various athletes/teams. Manage, organize, and maintain assigned athletic training rooms, equipment, supplies, and inventory. Assist in the preparation/breakdown of practices/competitions related to athletic training services. Communicate with sports medicine staff and its inter-professional members assigned to athletic training rooms. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Commitment to student-athlete welfare and student development for the athletic training program; Ability to collect, interpret, and analyze data, and prepare reports. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, and staff. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Required Education Current UIW student approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study program Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications First Aid and/or CPR / AED Certification. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Monday- Friday 8am- 5pm. Some weekends and evenings to meet departmental goals. Physical Demands Ability to lift, push, pull, or carry objects up to 30 pounds. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1676PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine Salary $11.00/hr Open Date 08/19/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
