    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31391": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Pharmaceutics Lab Grader Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Pharmaceutics Lab Grader Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Pharmaceutics Lab Grader Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The pharmaceutics lab grader will assist the pharmaceutics lab faculty with grading of lab assignments.The pharmaceutics lab grader reports to the Assistant Dean and Chair, Dept. of Pharm. Sc. This is a student position open to current UIW P3 pharmacy students. Essential Functions Essential duties include: The student grader will grade pre-and post- laboratory assignments in pharmaceutics laboratories. The grader will be responsible to pick up and return the assignments from a designated location. The grader will use the grading rubric provided by the faculty member to grade the assignments and will enter the grades into Canvas. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Ability to apply grading criteria or rubric uniformly to all assignments Complete grading duties in a timely manner Communicate effectively with course faculty Good time-management skills to ensure promptness in grading the weekly assignments and entering grades. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures; Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA Required Education Current UIW Feik School of Pharmacy P3 student. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Cumulative GPA of 3.5 or above. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Flexible hours up to a maximum of 4 hours per week. Physical Demands None. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1629PO Number of Vacancies 2 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Dean and Chair, Dept. of Pharm. Sc. Salary $12/hr Open Date 07/08/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you or will you be a FSOP P3 student? Yes No 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
