      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Men&#39;s Club Basketball Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Men's Club Basketball Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Men's Club Basketball Coach (Graduate Assistant) (Student) Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Men’s Club Basketball Coach (Graduate Assistant) is responsible for coaching the Men’s Club Sports Basketball team during the Fall and Spring semesters. This position reports to the Director of Sports and Wellness in the Club Sports Program. This is a student position open to UIW graduate students. Essential Functions Essential duties include: Attending all meetings, directing practices, training athletes on game strategies and techniques, motivating student-athletes, and supervising traveling, pre-game warmups, and games. Responsible for keeping balanced budgets and ensuring that student-athletes are maintaining their GPA . Help run and lead fundraising events, create new relationships with sponsors as well as attend community service events. Work with Club Sports supervisor to better the program by, but not limited to, assisting with marketing/ recruiting for Men’s Basketball team. Annual review following each season worked. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Knowledge of Men’s Basketball at the collegiate level. Ability to plan practices involving on-court instruction and player development. Commitment to student-athlete welfare and academic success. Commitment to University rules. Ability to assess team needs and develop goal-oriented action plans. Excellent organizational and time-management skills. Excellent marketing skills. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW graduate student Required Work Experience At least one (1) year coaching experience or participation in a college basketball program Preferred Qualifications None. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations CPR and First Aid Certification (if expired, must be completed within 3 months of employment) Work Hours 20 hours per week required. Practices and games/tournaments are on nights and weekends, ability to meet during work hours with athletes, trainer and supervisors during the academic year. Physical Demands Typical with job position. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1617PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness Salary Tuition Waiver and $13.00 per hour over 20 hours, up to 25 hours Open Date 07/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents 