    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31581": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Worker Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Worker Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Office of Communication and Brand Marketing is looking for a work study student to support the office and its staff. Students in this position may be required to work independently and with minimal supervision on projects. This position reports to the department’s Administrative Assistant. This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment. Essential Functions Answer the phones, greet guests, and represent the Office of Communications and Brand Marketing in a professional manner in the absence of the communications and brand marketing team. File, copy, and scan documents for team members. Review and archive newspapers, daily. Post University events to online community calendars and chamber of commerce newsletters and calendars. Run errands on campus, as needed. Assist with special event preparation, as needed. Take photographs at events, and as needed, throughout campus. Drive the golf cart in accordance with University and department guidelines. This may include opportunities to work on special projects remotely. Support the Office of Communications and Brand Marketing in events and projects including Light the Way and Commencement. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities To serve as a role model to the university community by acting with professionalism, through all phone, email, and in-person interactions with faculty, staff, administrators, students, and others. To work with discretion at all times. A confidentiality agreement will be signed, and if the terms of that are violated in any way, it is grounds for the immediate termination of the work-study assignment. To comply with all tasks and responsibilities laid out in the job description, and be willing and able to work on assigned duties as needed; Excellent problem-solving and customer service/phone skills. To work independently and manage time and responsibility expectations. Experience with Microsoft applications, including Word and PowerPoint; Familiar with using the internet and OneDrive; Willingness and ability to learn new computer programs. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Must be a current, undergraduate student at UIW . Current UIW student approved and eligible to participate in the Federal Work-Study program. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working in office support or customer service. Bilingual. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Must have a valid drivers license, driving record that is insurable by UIW insurance carrier, and be at least 21 years of age, as required to drive for UIW . Work Hours General availability during normal business hours, Monday – Friday, 8 am – 5 pm. May work up to 20 hours per week. Work schedule to be determined, based on student schedule. Some evenings and weekends when needed. Physical Demands Must be able to life 25 pounds Must be able to sit or stand for long periods of time. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1669PO Number of Vacancies 3 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to VP of Communications and Marketing Salary $11.00/hr Open Date 08/04/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
