    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31594": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Research Associate Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Research Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. N/A. Position Details Position Information Position Title Research Associate UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Research Associate is responsible for assisting in faculty-led research, operating and maintaining scientific instrumentation, coordinating research activities, contributing to the teaching and training of students and research personnel, and ensuring compliance with research regulations and procedures for the Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences. The role exercises independent judgment in troubleshooting experiments, supporting data integrity, and assisting with compliance‑related procedures under faculty direction. The Research Associate reports to the Assistant Dean/Chair of Pharmaceutical Sciences. Note that this position is institutional funded, not dependent on grant-funding. Benefits UIW has been identified year after year as one of the nation’s Great Colleges to Work For based on employee feedback. UIW offers an outstanding benefits package for full-time employees that includes medical, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts, numerous paid holidays, vacation and sick leave. Tuition benefits include UIW tuition waivers, tuition exchange programs and Brainpower Connection discounts for employees and dependents. Retirement benefits include 403b retirement plans with a 7% employer match, plus a retirement health solution. We also offer employer-paid Life/AD&D, long-term disability, pet insurance, an Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ), wellness programs, employee discount program, Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligibility and more! Please refer to the Human Resources webpage for additional details on our benefits and eligibility. Job Duties Job Duty Name Essential Duties Description of Job Duties Perform experiments across diverse research settings (animal studies, cell culture, chemistry) under faculty guidance. Communicate effectively with PIs regarding project timelines, expectations, and progress. Manage multiple concurrent research projects. Mentor, monitor and provide functional supervision of students and research personnel to ensure productivity, safety, and regulatory compliance. Coordinate and oversee day‑to‑day activities of research personnel executing study protocols. Train student, faculty, and external research users on proper operation and care of laboratory instruments; maintain training logs. Plan, initiate, and implement research study protocols, operating procedures, and data collection processes. Independently troubleshoot experiments, resolve laboratory issues, and ensure data integrity. Oversee data management to ensure high‑quality, timely, and well‑organized results. Operate, maintain, and troubleshoot laboratory equipment (e.g., LC‑MS, microtome, spectrophotometers, microscopes, incubators). Maintain supply inventories and obtain procurement quotes as needed. Participate in instruction of team‑taught laboratory courses. Document research‑related correspondence and equipment communication. Collaborate and communicate with faculty and student researchers. Assist with posters, manuscripts, grant writing, and related scholarly activities. Engage in professional development, seminars, and workshops to maintain current scientific practices. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Proficiency in MS Outlook, Word, Excel, and related administrative or data‑management systems. Strong verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills for effective interaction with PIs, faculty, students, and technical personnel. Excellent knowledge of laboratory sciences, including animal research, cell culture, chemistry‑based methods, and research protocol/safety regulations. Strong organizational, documentation, and time‑management skills to support multiple concurrent projects. Ability to understand and perform procedures and experiments within areas of formal training, and willingness to learn new techniques and instrumentation. Ability to train, mentor, and provide functional supervision of students and research personnel, on equipment use and laboratory best practices. Ability to work independently and collaboratively while supporting diverse research needs and engaging effectively with individuals from varied backgrounds. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Bachelors Degree in Chemistry, Biology, Pharmaceutical Science or a related field. Required Work Experience At least two (2) years of experience in a scientific research laboratory. Preferred Qualifications MS. in Biology, Chemistry, Pharmaceutical Sciences, or related field. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None specified. Work Hours Monday through Friday 8am to 5pm with flexibility and/or extended hours as needed to meet departmental goals. Some flexibility in schedule necessary due to nature of experiments. Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 20 lbs of research equipment or supplies. Ability to reach overhead, bend, and squat to retrieve laboratory materials. Ability to climb stools and/or ladders to reach top shelves. Dexterity to use laboratory equipment and tools. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number AS2292PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Full Time Job Category Administrator (exempt) Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Dean and Chair for Pharmaceutical Sciences Salary $45,000 - $52,000 Annualized Open Date 08/05/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant N/A. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Title IX This position is considered a “Responsible Employee” under Title IX federal regulations and “Mandatory Reporter” under Texas state law and the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. As a Mandatory Reporter, this position requires you as the employee to promptly report any incident that you witness or receive information about Title IX violations. These reporting responsibilities are set out in the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Professional Reference Contacts Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UIW Website HigherEdJobs.com Indeed LinkedIn WorkplaceDiversity.com HispanicDiversity.com BlackJobCenter.com WomensJobCenter.com VeteransConnect.com Personal Referral Employee Referral Other If you selected other, please tell us where? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least a Bachelor's Degree in Chemistry, Biology, Pharmaceutical Science or a related field? No Yes * How many years of experience do you have working in a scientific research laboratory? Less than 2 years 2 years 3 years 4 or more years 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/30988": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Small Interactive Groups Facilitator, Part-time Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Small Interactive Groups Facilitator, Part-time Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty in designated area as needed during the 2026-2027 Academic Year. Position Details Position Information Position Title Small Interactive Groups Facilitator, Part-time Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The University of the Incarnate Word School of Osteopathic Medicine ( UIWSOM ) invites part-time faculty candidates for Small Interactive Groups Facilitator. This position is responsible for guiding and evaluating the SIGS process. Small Group Interactive Sessions ( SIGS ) are a cornerstone of the first two years of UIWSOM’s Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) curriculum. During the first two years, learners meet on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday mornings in small groups with a faculty process facilitator. Candidates who are selected for the position must successfully complete the SIGS facilitator training program. In all matters, faculty are expected to maintain the highest standards of professional ethics consistent with the UIW Mission. This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty in designated area as needed during the 2026-2027 Academic Year. Benefits This position is not benefits eligible. Essential Functions Guide a group of 8-10 learners in the SIGS process to ensure the boundaries of the session are followed. Follow up with reflection questions as appropriate. Conduct performative and summative evaluations of learners. Attend SIGS facilitator debriefs. Work collaboratively with departmental faculty to ensure standard curriculum outcomes are met. Conduct respectful relationships with faculty, staff, and students both in and outside the classroom. Maintain contact with the department chair and participate in meetings upon request. Adhere to UIW policies and procedures. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Strong communication skills, verbal, written, and interpersonal. Strong collaboration, team building, problem-solving, conflict resolution, and analytical skills. Strong organizational skills. Ability to deliver instruction in person. Ability to effectively learn, use, and incorporate instructional technology into teaching. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Master’s Degree in any education or health profession field. Required Work Experience None. Preferred Qualifications Experience in small group facilitation. Doctoral level or terminal degree. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None specified. Work Hours 8-10 hours per week. Monday, Wednesday, and Friday mornings. Physical Demands None specified. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number UN1024PO Number of Vacancies 3 Job Type Part Time Job Category Faculty Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Lori Kels, Chair, Department of Clinical Sciences Salary tba Open Date 05/11/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant This applicant pool will remain online and be used to hire interested part-time faculty in designated area as needed during the 2026-2027 Academic Year. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Title IX This position is considered a “Responsible Employee” under Title IX federal regulations and “Mandatory Reporter” under Texas state law and the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. As a Mandatory Reporter, this position requires you as the employee to promptly report any incident that you witness or receive information about Title IX violations. These reporting responsibilities are set out in the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV (Faculty) Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts 1 Professional Reference Contacts Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UIW Website HigherEdJobs.com Indeed LinkedIn WorkplaceDiversity.com HispanicDiversity.com BlackJobCenter.com WomensJobCenter.com VeteransConnect.com Personal Referral Employee Referral Other If you selected other, please tell us where? (Open Ended Question) * What is the highest level of education you have achieved from an accredited institution? Less than Master's Degree Master's Degree Doctorate Degree * Describe your experience, if any,  in small group facilitation. (Open Ended Question) 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31439": {
      "title": "RLHO Office Assistant-Student",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | RLHO Office Assistant-Student Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW RLHO Office Assistant-Student Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title RLHO Office Assistant-Student Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Student Office Assistant for the Department of Residence Life and Housing Operations provides administrative support, to include: filing; working on assigned projects; tours; and assisting with the daily operations of the offices. The Student Office Assistant reports to the Associate Director of Residence Life and HOusing Operations Essential Functions Works on different tasks as assigned by the Residence Life Administrative Team to include, but not limited to: Filing student paperwork. Making ID cards. Providing desk coverage within offices. Responding to guest inquiries. Performing lockouts. Performing hall tours. Developing marketing materials, etc. Performing other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Ability to converse clearly on the phone. Work in a team-driven environment. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA Required Education Current UIW student. Required Work Experience N/A. Preferred Qualifications N/A. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations N/A. Work Hours The Student Assistant will provide office assistance during normal business hours between 8:00 am and 5:00 pm, however, will not work more than 20 hours a week. Certain evening hours and weekend hours may be scheduled due to office commitments. Some evening and weekend hours to include one Saturday per month Physical Demands This position requires light lifting and the ability to navigate campus. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1632PO Number of Vacancies 1-2 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Associate Director of Residence Life and Housing Operations Salary $11/hr Open Date 07/14/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
