    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31335": {
      "title": "Wellness Center Technician (Graduate Assistant)",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Wellness Center Technician (Graduate Assistant) Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Wellness Center Technician (Graduate Assistant) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Wellness Center Technician (Graduate Assistant) Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Wellness Center Technician (Graduate Assistant) for the Wellness Center is the technician supervisor and is responsible for completing maintenance and repairs of equipment and facility Wellness Center. Duties for this position include daily cleaning of facility, equipment, and dressing rooms and overseeing technician staff. The Wellness Center Technician (Graduate Assistant) reports to the Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness. Essential Functions Essential functions include: Complete scheduled walkthrough as assigned by the Director and Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness. Schedule repairs and maintenance (outsourced and in-house). Schedule student technician staff. Supervise the student technician staff. Assist the Assistant Director and Director in the interview process of student technician staff. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Good customer relation and service skills. Ability to work in a team and as an individual in a self-paced, task-oriented environment. Very detail-oriented. Ability to be organized and cleanly. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Ability to understand fitness equipment and how to make basic repairs. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW graduate student. Required Work Experience One (1) or more years of work experience in the fitness and wellness industry. Working knowledge of fitness equipment and tools. Supervisory experience. Preferred Qualifications None. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Current CPR and First Aid Certification (if expired, must be completed within 3 months of employment) Work Hours Hours are flexible with work completed during open facility hours. Must be available openings, weekends and evenings and be on-call as duties required. Will be required to cover holiday and school break schedules as required by the Director and Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness. Required to work 20 hours per week. Physical Demands This position requires manual labor with the ability to lift 50 pounds. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1622PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Director of Sports and Wellness Salary Tuition Waiver and $13.00 per hour over 20 hours, up to 25 hours Open Date 07/06/2026 Close Date 05/31/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Letter of R