s to help students learn and answer their questions (1 hour per 3-hour class, physically and/or virtually). Adhere to UIW Faculty Handbook policies and procedures, including timely record keeping of student activities, fair and equitable evaluation of student performance, and timely feedback to students regarding their performance in the course. Conduct respectful relationships with faculty, staff, and students both in and outside the classroom. Maintain contact with the academic affairs team and participate in meetings upon request. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Ability to deliver instruction online and in-person. Ability to effectively learn, use, and incorporate instructional technology into teaching. Willingness and flexibility to teach day, evening, and weekend sections as needed. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Doctorate Degree/Terminal Degree with 18 graduate semester hours in relevant science discipline is required to teach graduate courses. Master’s Degree with 18 graduate hours in relevant science discipline is required to teach undergraduate courses. Required Work Experience One (1) year of professional experience in a biology field. Experience teaching adult learners. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching at the collegiate level. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None specified. Work Hours Based on course assignment. Physical Demands Typical for faculty in this discipline. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number UN1049PO Number of Vacancies 3 Job Type Part Time Job Category Faculty Desired Start Date Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Executive Director, School of Professional Studies Salary $1250 - $3500 per online class based on student count; $2450 per in-person c