    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31545": {
      "title": "Video Production Assistant",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Video Production Assistant Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Video Production Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. None. Position Details Position Information Position Title Video Production Assistant Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Video Production Assistant is responsible for producing the live streaming and coverage of all home UIW athletic events. This includes the setup and take down of equipment and producing a quality stream while incorporating all sponsorship assets. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Office of Communications and Brand Marketing. Essential Functions Assist in production of streams for all UIW home events including football, baseball, basketball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, volleyball, swim and dive, and others as requested. Assist with the video board and game entertainment for football and assisting with social media highlights and preproduction elements. Assist in the production of additional UIW features as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Must be a self-starter and have the ability to work without supervision. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Knowledge of broadcast equipment and the structure of a live broadcast. Exemplify a go getter attitude and willingness to support the greater good of the team. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference and the NCAA . Required Education Current UIW Student. Required Work Experience Experience with Adobe Creative Cloud, video cameras, Tri-Caster, or 3 Play. Preferred Qualifications Experience in any of the following: graphic design, video editing, photography, audio technician, and/or camera operating. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours Monday thru Friday 8am – 5pm. Must be willing to work nights and weekends. Physical Demands Ability to lift equipment, tools, and/or materials weighing up to 25 pounds waist high. May be required to stand for extended periods of time. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1665PO Number of Vacancies 14 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Multi-Hire Pool Yes Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to Assistant Director, Office of Communications and Brand Marketing Salary $11.00/hr Open Date 07/29/2026 Close Date 05/15/2027 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant None. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't