    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31252": {
      "title": "CRNA Program Recruitment and Compliance Specialist",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | CRNA Program Recruitment and Compliance Specialist Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW CRNA Program Recruitment and Compliance Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. N/A. Position Details Position Information Position Title CRNA Program Recruitment and Compliance Specialist UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The CRNA Program Recruitment and Compliance Specialist will play a pivotal role in driving the growth and success of the CRNA program by effectively managing the recruitment, enrollment and compliance processes from initial inquiries to successful matriculation of graduate registered nurses. The role encompasses building clinical partnerships, marketing and social media engagement, credentialing and compliance for all external and internal agencies as well as facilitating student clinical rotation schedules and monitoring program compliance with accreditation standards. This dynamic position works closely with CRNA program administration to collect, monitor, analyze and synthesize data for program outcomes. The CRNA Program Recruitment and Compliance Specialist reports to the CRNA Program Director. Benefits UIW has been identified year after year as one of the nation’s Great Colleges to Work For based on employee feedback. UIW offers an outstanding benefits package for full-time employees that includes medical, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts, numerous paid holidays, vacation and sick leave. Tuition benefits include UIW tuition waivers, tuition exchange programs and Brainpower Connection discounts for employees and dependents. Retirement benefits include 403b retirement plans with a 7% employer match, plus a retirement health solution. We also offer employer-paid Life/AD&D, long-term disability, pet insurance, an Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ), wellness programs, employee discount program, Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) eligibility and more! Please refer to the Human Resources webpage for additional details on our benefits and eligibility. Job Duties Job Duty Name Essential Job Functions Description of Job Duties Independently reviews and evaluates admission documents, specifically transcripts and degree certificates to determine if an applicant’s educational background has met the admission criteria for the program. Provides timely articulations. Researches compliance concerns (student certifications and licensures) and reports findings to the CRNA Program Director for strategic program planning. Collaborates with University departments to facilitate timely and effective communication with students (Admissions office, financial aid, student health). Manages and tracks student records in program software. Schedules tours for prospective students and assists with onboarding students to UIW policies and procedures. Provides support for orientation, admissions, graduation and special events for the CRNA program (pinning ceremony, white coat ceremony). Schedules, manages and attends marketing events and exhibits to promote program initiatives and student recruitment. Maintains the prospective student databases for accreditation standards. Distributes surveys, and collects/maintains data for program outcomes and assessments. Communicates with alumni base to market program events and attendance. Travels to represent UIW CRNA program at local, state and national recruitment fairs and conferences. Updates the webpages and all branding and marketing materials for the CRNA program. Creates educational marketing publications, newsletters and social media announcements to provide current program events and trends. Conducts live and web-mediated information sessions for student recruitment. Builds clinical partnerships to ensure timely student credentialing for clinical rotations. Reviews and maintains background checks, immunizations, student medical insurance documents and waivers. Participates in faculty, staff and clinical team meetings. Maintains all clinical rotation schedules and student portraits by cohort for the program. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Strong proficiency in Microsoft Office Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, Word and Microsoft Teams. Strong skills in teamwork, collaboration and marketing. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to manage sensitive student communications. Excellent organizational and prioritization skills with attention to detail. Ability to work effectively in interprofessional team environment with internal and external stakeholders. Strong presentation skills in live and web-mediated sessions. Knowledge of CRNA scope of practice and national accreditation standards for nursing and nurse anesthesiology. Experience troubleshooting data management hiccups. Experience working in an academic setting. Ability to receive and provide feedback related to program outcomes. Experience with posting responsibly on social media platforms and updating websites for the program to meet accreditation requirements. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference, and the NCAA . Required Education Bachelor’s Degree in Healthcare/Education or relevant field. Required Work Experience Two (2) years of professional office and/or managerial experience in a complex office environment. Preferred Qualifications N/A. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations Must have a valid driver’s license, driving record that is insurable by UIW insurance carrier, and be at least 21 years of age, as required to drive for UIW . Id must have “real id” designation as required for air travel. Work Hours Monday through Friday 8am to 5pm with extended hours as needed, especially in the planning and execution of events, to meet departmental goals. Physical Demands Ability to lift up to 15lbs for table set-up/tear-down at events, as well as carry office supplies. Ability to reach overhead, bend, squat to retrieve office/events materials. Ability to push/pull event carts holding up to 50 lbs. Ability to actively engage in events for extended periods of time. Ability to regularly move about campus and event venues to actively engage faculty, staff, and potential/current residents, as well as attend meetings on and off campus. Ability to navigate airports with recruitment materials. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number AS2271PO Number of Vacancies 1 Job Type Full Time Job Category Administrator (exempt) Desired Start Date 07/16/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to CRNA Program Director Salary $55,000-$58,000 Annualized Open Date 06/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant N/A. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Title IX This position is considered a “Responsible Employee” under Title IX federal regulations and “Mandatory Reporter” under Texas state law and the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. As a Mandatory Reporter, this position requires you as the employee to promptly report any incident that you witness or receive information about Title IX violations. These reporting responsibilities are set out in the UIW Sexual Misconduct Policy. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UIW Website HigherEdJobs.com Indeed LinkedIn WorkplaceDiversity.com HispanicDiversity.com BlackJobCenter.com WomensJobCenter.com VeteransConnect.com Personal Referral Employee Referral Other If you selected other, please tell us where? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least a Bachelor’s Degree in Healthcare/Education or relevant field? No Yes, Bachelor’s Degree in Healthcare/Education Yes, Bachelor’s Degree in relevant field * How many years of professional office and/or managerial experience in a complex office environment? Less than 2 years 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 or more years * Do you currently have a valid driver's license AND are you at least 21 years of age, as required to drive for UIW? No Yes, I have a valid driver license and I am at least 21 years old * Do you currently have a valid driver license with \"Real Id\" designation as required for air travel? No Yes * List the Microsoft Office products with which you are experienced.  Include your proficiency level in each and include special skills in each, where applicable. Examples of proficiency levels-None, Minimal, Limited, Proficient, Advanced, Expert.  Examples of special skills:  MS Outlook-mail merges; MS Excel-V-lookup & pivot tables. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience conducting presentations. Specify the frequency as well as audience type (employees, visitors, students, etc...) and number to which you presented. (Open Ended Question) 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uiw.edu/postings/31615": {
      "title": "Student Assistant for Student Engagement Center",
      "description": "University of the Incarnate Word - Cardinal Talent | Student Assistant for Student Engagement Center Skip to Main Content Cardinal Talent Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help UIW Home UIW Strategic Priorities Visit UIW Student Assistant for Student Engagement Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit class schedule, and preferred days/times. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Assistant for Student Engagement Center Academic Year 2026-2027 UIW Mission University of the Incarnate Word is a Catholic institution that welcomes to its community persons of diverse backgrounds, in the belief that their respectful interaction advances the discovery of truth, mutual understanding, self-realization, and the common good. Position Summary The Student Assistant for the Student Engagement Center ( SEC ) assists the SEC Staff with event management, the SEC Information Desk, and the Red’s Pub Check-Out Desk within the Student Engagement Center. The Student Assistant reports to the Events Operating Manager. This is a student position open to current UIW students who may be hired through the Federal Work-Study Program or student employment. Essential Functions Set up and break down of rooms in the Student Engagement Center, including SEC Ballroom and meeting rooms. Set up and break down of audio/visual equipment. Staff the SEC Info Desk, to provide helpful information. Staff the Red’s Pub Check Out Desk, to check out games. Customer service to all who come into the SEC . Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Knowledge Skills and Abilities Good attitude. Ability to communicate with customers and other employees. Willingness to be a team player. Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures; Employee shall adhere to all applicable rules and regulations of the University, the Conference and the NCAA . Required Education Currently enrolled UIW student. Required Work Experience Previous work experience is not required. Training is available for setups, break downs, gaming equipment, and audio/visual knowledge. Preferred Qualifications None. Required Certifications, Licenses or Registrations None. Work Hours As a group, the students staff the Student Engagement Center 8am-10pm, daily; Must have night and weekend availability; Please note: Each student will have a regular weekly work schedule and have the opportunity to pick up additional hours as the event load allows. Students must work 10 hours per week, but not more than 20 hours per week. Physical Demands Ability to lift and carry 25 lbs, for room setups and tear downs of tables, chairs, gaming equipment and audio/visual equipment. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number STU1670PO Number of Vacancies 3 Job Type Part Time Job Category Students Desired Start Date 08/24/2026 Multi-Hire Pool No Position End Date (if temporary) Reports to SEC FACILITY AND EVENTS OPERATIONS MANAGER Salary $11.00/HR Open Date 08/11/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Please submit class schedule, and preferred days/times. EOE UIW is committed to a policy of equal opportunity in employment, without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, citizenship status, national origin, age, marital status, disability, genetic information, gender identity or expression, veteran status, pregnancy, and religion (except in limited circumstances when religious preference is both permitted by law and deemed appropriate as a matter of University policy). Applicant Documents Required Documents Student Class Schedule Optional Documents Resume Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UIW student? Yes, I am a doctoral student Yes, I am a graduate student Yes, I am a senior Yes, I am a junior Yes, I am a sophomore Yes, I am a freshman No, I am not a UIW student * Are you eligible for Financial Aid and approved to participate in the Federal Work Study program? yes no I don't know 4301 Broadway, San Antonio, Texas 78209 210-829-6000 • 1-800-749-WORD Back to top © 2019. University of the Incarnate Word. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
